==Trivia==
*Abyss Gazers may be named after one of [[wikipedia:Friedrich Nietzsche|Friedrich Nietszche]]'s famous quotes, "And if you gaze long into the abyss, the abyss gazes also into you."
**It may also be a reference to the [[wikia:darksouls:Abyss Watchers|Abyss Watchers]], a boss from the game ''[[wikia:darksouls:Dark Souls III|Dark Souls III]]''.
*All three remake stages' Japanese names are inversions of their [[Squishy Cave]] counterparts:
**[[Deadly Weapons]]' Japanese name, Gachigachi Ankoku Heiki (ガチガチ暗黒兵器, "Rigid Dark Weapon"), is the opposite of [[Fluffy Dark Weapon]].
**[[Inspirational Mural]]'s Japanese name, Kawaii Hekiga (かわいい壁画, "Cute Mural"), implies the opposite of the scarier [[Mural of the Devil]].
**[[Murmuring Evil]]'s Japanese name, Gessori Seiakusetsu (ゲッソリ性悪説, "Emaciated Theory of Fundamental Evil), is the opposite of [[Chubby B. Goode]]'s Japanese name, Potchari Seizensetsu (ぽっちゃり性善説, "Chubby Theory of Fundamental Kindness").

